== README.org as Markdown, its first 12 lines of HTML
<ul><li>chez-sodium</li></ul>
<p>Password hashing, random bytes and fast hashing for Chez Scheme, through
[[https://doc.libsodium.org/][libsodium]]'s C library.</p>
<p>#+begin_quote
✨ <em>AI Disclosure:</em> LLMs are used extensively in the planning and development of this project.
#+end_quote</p>
<p>chez-sodium will bind a small part of =libsodium= through Chez's foreign
interface, and load it when your program runs: there will be nothing to
compile. It covers four jobs:</p>
<ul><li>hash a password with argon2id, check it, and tell when a hash needs
redoing because its limits were raised;</li><li>make random bytes from the system, for keys and tokens;</li><li>hash bytes fast with BLAKE2b, for storing a long random key without storing
the key;</li><li>compare two secrets in constant time.</li></ul>
